  ],
  "description": {
   "en": "\"If you're going to put your life and body on the line, then you better put it on the line!\" - Kan'ichi Douda, a man of great courage and a loud voice, is the head of the cheerleading squad for a major general contractor. He's popular for his bold personality, but when the baseball team disbands, he's the first to be laid off. His boss, who has his eye on his body, casts him in the role of a dirty negotiator with the Yakuza! This is the start of a huge collaboration between the story of negotiation skills by Shinji Makari, author of \"Yugo,\" and the \"warmth of a man\" by Kei Sadayasu, author of \"Aa Harima Nada,\" which will touch your heart!"
  },
